      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the geometry switch needs the reserved TTBR0 first: since aosp/4312469, `check_and_switch_context()` changes TG0/T0SZ while TTBR0 still points at the previous mm\u0027s tables, unless CnP or PAN emulation has already installed the reserved one. `mm_tcr_needs_switch()` and its stub also sit in the right `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` block.\n\nWould you mind moving the sequence, comment included, into `mm_switch_tcr()` in `arch/arm64/include/asm/p3s/mmu.h`? Then `check_and_switch_context()` keeps its existing one-line `mm_switch_tcr(mm);` hook and `context.c` doesn\u0027t change at all. Something like:\n\n```\n#define mm_switch_tcr(mm)\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\ndo {\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n\tif (mm_tcr_needs_switch(mm)) {\t\t\t\t\t\\\n\t\tcpu_set_reserved_ttbr0();\t\t\t\t\\\n\t\tlocal_flush_tlb_all();\t\t\t\t\t\\\n\t\t__cpu_set_tcr_geometry(mm_tcr_geometry(mm));\t\t\\\n\t}\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n} while (0)\n```\n\nIt needs to stay a macro, since `\u003casm/mmu_context.h\u003e` includes this header before it defines `cpu_set_reserved_ttbr0()`. The call in `cpu_do_switch_mm()` would get the same ordering too: there the TCR write only follows `cpu_set_reserved_ttbr0_nosync()`, which as far as I know isn\u0027t ordered against it without an ISB (upstream `b9293d457ff3` only relies on TTBR0/TTBR1 writes being ordered among themselves).",
